      <FactsAndCircumstancesTestTxt>FACT AND CIRCUMSTANCES FOR PUBLIC SUPPORT THE ENERGY FOR GROWTH HUB WAS FOUNDED IN 2018 AS A 501(C)(3) NOT-FOR-PROFIT CORPORATION TO REDUCE GLOBAL POVERTY AND PROMOTE ECONOMIC OPPORTUNITY BY USING RESEARCH AND DATA TO IMPROVE THE PROVISION AND QUALITY OF ELECTRICITY IN POOR REGIONS OF THE WORLD, ESPECIALLY IN AFRICA AND ASIA.THE ENERGY FOR GROWTH HUB IS ORGANIZED AND OPERATED TO ATTRACT NEW AND ADDITIONAL PUBLIC SUPPORT AND FUNDING ON A CONTINUOUS BASIS. THE ORGANIZATION MAINTAINS AN ONGOING PROGRAM FOR SOLICITATION OF FUNDS FROM PUBLIC CHARITIES, PHILANTHROPIC ORGANIZATIONS, CORPORATIONS, AND INDIVIDUALS. IT MEETS THE FACTS AND CIRCUMSTANCES TEST BY THE FOLLOWING: 1. THE PERCENTAGE OF PUBLIC SUPPORT IS CURRENTLY AT 29.74%, WHICH IS ABOVE THE 10 PERCENT THRESHOLD. 2. THE ORGANIZATION IS ACTIVELY AND CONTINUALLY SEEKING TO GROW ITS PUBLIC SUPPORT BASE. IN 2024, THE ORGANIZATION ADDED TWO NEW PHILANTHROPIC FUNDING SOURCES, BRINGING THE TOTAL TO ELEVEN, REPRESENTING A WIDE VARIETY OF INTERESTS IN GLOBAL POVERTY, HUMAN WELL BEING, ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT, TECHNOLOGY, CLIMATE CHANGE, AND US NATIONAL SECURITY. AN EXPANSION IN THE ORGANIZATION'S FUNDING BASE IS EXPECTED TO CONTINUE IN THE FUTURE, WITH ACTIVE DISCUSSIONS UNDERWAY WITH ADDITIONAL NEW PHILANTHROPIC FUNDING ORGANIZATIONS. IN 2022, THE ORGANIZATION ALSO BEGAN EXPANDED SOLICITATION OF INDIVIDUALS, WITH THE FIRST SUCCESSFUL INDIVIDUAL DONATIONS RECEIVED IN EARLY 2023. IN MAY 2023, THE ORGANIZATION ALSO LAUNCHED A NEW WEBSITE WITH A DONATE LINK OPTION FOR PUBLIC SOLICITATION. 3. THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE ORGANIZATION IS THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS, COMPOSED OF NINE TRUSTEES WITH A DIVERSE RANGE OF BACKGROUNDS AND REPRESENTING A BROAD RANGE OF COMMUNITY EXPERTISE INCLUDING PUBLIC FINANCE, BUSINESS, PHILANTHROPY, PUBLIC POLICY, AND TECHNOLOGY. THE BOARD ALSO INCLUDES FOUR DISTINGUISHED HONORARY MEMBERS WHO ARE DRAWN FROM PUBLIC SERVICE, THE UNITED NATIONS, AND ACADEMIA. 4. THE ENERGY FOR GROWTH HUB ENGAGES IN A VARIETY OF RESEARCH AND ACTIVITIES DIRECTLY FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE GENERAL PUBLIC ON A CONTINUING BASIS. ITS PROGRAMS AND ACTIVITIES HAVE BROAD APPEAL TO MEMBERS OF THE PUBLIC AROUND THE WORLD THAT SHARE AN INTEREST IN THE PROMOTION OF CLEAN RELIABLE ENERGY FOR EVERYONE. THE ORGANIZATION PUBLISHES ITS RESEARCH, REPORTS, AND FINDINGS ON ITS OWN WEBSITE, WHICH IS USED BY UNIVERSITIES, PUBLIC AGENCIES, AND THE GENERAL PUBLIC. MEMBERS OF THE STAFF REGULARLY PROVIDE GUEST LECTURES AT UNIVERSITIES, PARTICIPATE IN UNIVERSITY-BASED RESEARCH PROJECTS, AND SPONSOR CAPSTONE RESEARCH PROJECTS. THE ORGANIZATION'S EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR IS AN AFFILIATED SCHOLAR AT RICE UNIVERSITY AND THE COLORADO SCHOOL OF MINES, WHILE NINE OF OUR FELLOWS ARE UNIVERSITY FACULTY. THE ORGANIZATION'S NEWSLETTER IS FREE TO THE PUBLIC AND HAS OVER 1,300 SUBSCRIBERS. ALTHOUGH THE ORGANIZATION DOES NOT HOST IN-PERSON EVENTS, IT ORGANIZES OCCASIONAL ONLINE SEMINARS WHICH ARE POSTED ON THE WEBSITE, WHILE ITS PODCAST IS AVAILABLE FOR FREE ON ALL MAJOR PLATFORMS.</FactsAndCircumstancesTestTxt>
